Bug 1: Search doesn't include Alias, aka can't search for "Evo:" (should it though?, it's a bit pointless)

Bug 2: Trying to insert a new card throws an error page with:
"{"detail":[{"type":"int_parsing","loc":["path","card_id"],"msg":"Input should be a valid integer, unable to parse string as an integer","input":"new"}]}"

Bug 3: Why is there both a "Rule text" field and an "Abilities" field for cards & tokens when I try to update them? Especially since it seems they have the exact same information? Are there 2 separate columns in the DB? Because then I think one column should be dropped entirely

You misunderstood this fragment:
"k) the most important: parsing the "rules_text" field.
- The keywords have their own DB we will get to. I want you to extract all the keywords, nicely indicated by the <key> tag, and check it against the keyword DB, and if not existent, add it there
- Keywords should also still appear in the card data, but it should appear twice - once, in a specialized "Keywords" attributes, that should only contain links to the actual keywords in the db, stripped of their parameters - and secondly, they should still appear in the "abilities" attribute alongside other attributes, this time alongside their parameters.
- Other abilities in "rules_text" should appear in the "abilities" attribute"

What I meant was, from the input "rules_text" field in the input file, you should obtain the keywords and put them into a keyword ref attribute, and an abilities attribute that has both the keywords as they are currently presented and the other abilities. You shouldn't have 2 columns abilities and rules text.
Unless there is a meaningful difference between the 2 columns, in which case correct me, drop one of the columns.

Bug 4: When editing cards & tokens, doing so by the "Keyword IDs" is not useful, as I don't know them. In the edit page, I should be able to see & introduce the keyword words in that field, then have the UI translate it to IDs (and then they may be stored by their id or however the backend stores them). When I introduce a parameterized keyword such as "Ammo 2", link it to the actual keyword "Ammo <number>" as usual.

Bug 5: Minor, when I introduced for card X a related card named "Ackey The Archer", the UI correctly linked to the card I wanted named "Ackey the Archer". But as you see, that "the" is not capitalized, and while it links correctly, upon linking on X's detail page the related card is still "Ackey The Archer". Please upon linking also check if the names match in capitalization and auto-correct the related card name in capitalization (just capitalization, not misspells or anything else)

Card/token update feature seems to work well otherwise

Bug 6: Tokens shouldn't have a "Sets" attribute. You can outright drop that column, I don't need to store it at all.

Bug 7: Search doesn't also include the Related Cards field, the Sets field, design type field, if it's printed or not, can't search by P/T or by cost, color
In fact, the entire search functionality should be overhauled later down the line.
I would like to keep the current search bar, but also have an "Advanced Search" which opens a new page where I can search by inputting specific values for each value, aka I want that page to have prompts for all the fields, so I can input there whatever values I want.
Also, I would like some negation operator, that excludes terms if they have a - in front.
For example: Vigilance -Haste -"This enters tapped" should search for cards with Vigilance, but that lack Haste and that "This enters tapped" string.
But again, this should be done later, closer to the full UI. Mark it as a todo later "advanced search"

For now, at least include the Related Cards field & card types and subtypes, so you can search by name, creature types & subtypes, related cards, keywords & abilities (though the abilities field should include the keywords anyway) (also applies to tokens db search)

